Here is a task to complete. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(10);
Node b = new Node(25);
Node c = new Node(5);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

Analyze what happens in this case. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {4, 9, 11, 13, 18, 19, 24, 27, 28};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 11) return steps; if (a[mid] < 11) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return steps;

